  "query_preview": "/Friday through Tuesday/...\nThe upper level low looks to stall or drift slowly across the Pacific \nNorthwest through Friday before gradually weakening over the\nweekend. \n\nA prolonged period of rainfall through Friday evening is possible as \nthe main core of upper dynamics and plume of Pacific moisture cross \nsoutheast Oregon and southwest Idaho. Showers and embedded thunderstorms \nwill remain widespread. Close to half an inch of rainfall is possible, \nwith locally higher amounts Thursday through Friday. Persistent cloud \ncover and precipitation will keep Friday temperatures well below normal, \nwith valley highs only in the upper 60s to lower 70s.\n\nFor Saturday through Tuesday, the closed low will transition into an \nopen trough and move eastward toward the northern Rockies. While the \nheaviest and most widespread rain will shift east of our area by early \nSaturday, unsettled conditions will persist. Secondary shortwaves \nrotating through the trough will maintain daily chances (20 to 40 \npercent) for afternoon showers and isolated thunderstorms through early \nnext week, primarily over mountainous terrain. Temperatures will begin \na steady recovery over the weekend and into Tuesday, though remaining \nslightly below normal for early September.",
